`--output json` prints one indented array of objects, one object per row, each carrying the
file's frontmatter keys plus `path` and `slug`. Same fixture as
`yaml-output-carries-the-json-rows`, so the two formats are readable side by side.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/alpha/index.md --
---
title: Alpha
status: ready-for-dev
---

body
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/beta/index.md --
---
title: Beta
status: done
---

body
-- cmd --
booping query --glob 'plans/*/index.md' --output json
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
[
  {
    "title": "Alpha",
    "status": "ready-for-dev",
    "path": "plans/alpha/index.md",
    "slug": "alpha"
  },
  {
    "title": "Beta",
    "status": "done",
    "path": "plans/beta/index.md",
    "slug": "beta"
  }
]
-- stderr --
